evals.prompt:
Add a profile page at /users/:id. It shows the user's name, the posts they wrote, and the comments they wrote, each comment with the title of the post it is on.

The feed (src/pages/Feed.tsx) already loads `PostResource.getList` from `GET /api/posts`, which returns:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "1",
    "title": "My first post!",
    "author": { "id": "123", "name": "Paul" },
    "comments": [
      { "id": "249", "content": "Nice post!", "commenter": { "id": "245", "name": "Jane" } },
      { "id": "250", "content": "Thanks!", "commenter": { "id": "123", "name": "Paul" } }
    ]
  }
]
```

`GET /api/users/:id` returns only `{ "id", "name" }`. The API has no endpoint for a user's posts or comments, and we can't change the API. Opening a profile from the feed must not refetch the feed or make a request per post or comment. Resources are in src/resources/Post.ts.
